# L §3.6 The arrival rule: "Its law date is the event's: it states at m.day"; E §4.2 Steps 0-2 (2.1-C7b-11): the walk
# runs the arrival rule "its law at its movement's day (at m.day, LANGUAGE §3.6)", even for a leg with its own later
# on.  pay is dated 2026-02-20 and its leg lands on 2026-03-05; the rule's input sa is 1 under the law of February and 0
# from March.  The arrival is labelled by February's law: Ania's 100.00 (carried through), Tomek's 0.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind persons: parties
kind savings: place PLN min 0
  owned by arrive
  step minor(PLN)
  takes k for w prorata
place konto: savings lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input sa: num
input mday: date
input lday: date
input amt: money PLN
def arrive[m in events, p in parties]: num at m.day
  rule base = (if p == ania then sa else if p == tomek then 1 - sa else 0)

move pay: transfers
  on mday
  leg cash from world to konto amount amt on lday

ask q: bal(konto, 2026-03-31) of ania, bal(konto, 2026-03-31) of tomek

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  persons + [ania] lives 1980-01-01..
  persons + [tomek] lives 1981-01-01..
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  mday = 2026-02-20
  lday = 2026-03-05
  amt = 100.00 PLN

version feb
  cite s
  governs 2026-01..2026-02
  known 2026-01-01
  sa = 1

version mar
  cite s
  governs 2026-03..
  known 2026-01-01
  sa = 0
=== expect
q: (100.00 PLN, 0.00 PLN)
...
